- op: discuss  # 5e1a
  at: '2026-09-29T09:39:34Z'  # 5e1a
  by: agent  # 5e1a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5e1a
  clock: 6  # 5e1a
  nonce: 5e1a  # 5e1a
  message: "FIXED in PR #1296 (merged, dev da4ea54283). io_boundary.declared_by_an_included_header(language, name, system_includes): a translation unit that includes the header declaring a catalogued function calls THAT function -- a same-named definition in another file must match the prototype, so it is an interposer or a platform replacement of the same contract, and name resolution cannot see which the build links. Asked through the one row-choice rule (lookup_with_module over the include list). c.py and cpp.py (free calls only; member calls untouched) emit the catalogued unresolved call instead of the resolved edge when it holds; a definition in the CALLING file still wins.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev (the premise-check fixture): src/main.c getenv -> sendto beside lib/wamr/.../nuttx_platform.c stub sendto/recvfrom: verify-claims host_secret -> network was CONFIRMED (0 flows) on dev 8a1f82137a, now VIOLATED stdlib.getenv -> sys/socket.sendto; io-boundaries now net_send sys/socket.sendto + net_recv sys/socket.recvfrom (was env_read only). Control (no shim) unchanged: violated.\nMEASURED (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/rimon_09292026/RESULT.md): census 0 rebinding calls on 10 C repos; fluent-bit 486 calls newly classified, 0 lost (first-party net_send 0->31); whisper.cpp +11 io rows, all 11 read back as real libc calls; 11 other C/C++ repos: 0 verdict and 0 io changes.\nRULING COLLISION, SURFACED FOR THE OWNER: test_c_include_module_hint (WI-lajus) pinned the reverse -- a project send() in another file must capture a call whose file includes <sys/socket.h>. Its fixture is the stub-shim shape that produced the false all-clear, and its rationale called loosening that gate \"the false-all-clear direction\" when it is the recall direction. I split it: a send defined in the CALLING file still wins; the cross-file case now asserts the libc slot. Revert path if the owner disagrees: drop the declared_by_an_included_header guard in c.py/cpp.py and restore the old test.\nFiled in passing: WI-hilot (cpp <cstdlib>/<cstdio> spellings match no C row)."  # 5e1a
